title: Line Profile
keyword: LINE
manual: graphics/#c2-line

Plots the values of one or more fields of the system, their derivatives or arithmetic
expressions of the fields along a straight line between two points. Use it to inspect a bond
profile or the decay of a density away from a nucleus. The endpoints, the segment and a
cursor are drawn in the view while the window is open.

# Options

- "A" and "B": the two endpoints of the line, with their coordinates (fractional in a crystal,
  Å in a molecule). "Pick" lets you click each endpoint in the view: an atom, a critical
  point or a point in empty space. "Swap" exchanges the endpoints.
- "Points" (More): the number of points on the line, including the endpoints.
- "Curves": the quantities plotted. "Add Curve" adds a curve with the value of the reference
  field, which can then be changed. For each curve, the checkbox shows it in the plot, the
  color swatch sets its color and "Kind" chooses between a quantity of a field (value,
  gradient components, gradient norm, Hessian components or Laplacian) and an arithmetic
  expression of the fields (for instance "$1 - $2" or "$1:l"). The close icon removes a curve.
- "Value axis": linear, logarithmic or symmetric log, which is logarithmic away from zero and
  linear near it, for curves that change sign.

# Results

The "Plot" section draws the curves against the distance along the line. Drag the vertical
line in the plot to move the cursor: its distance "d" and the value of every shown curve
there are written under the plot, and the cursor is also drawn in the view.

"Values along the line" is a table with the position of each point, its distance from A and
the values of the curves. Right-click the header to choose which curves are listed, or to
copy the table or write it to a file.

# Notes

The curves are recalculated whenever the endpoints, the number of points or the curves
change. The window needs a system with atoms.
